---
import GuideArticle from '../../../../components/GuideArticle.astro';
import { routeOf, GUIDE_BASE, routeDetailHref, hasRouteDetail, canonicalRouteSummaryOf } from '../../../../data/phone.js';

const club = routeOf('clubsim-sms-pack-6hkd-2026');
const sosim = routeOf('sosim-recharge-ladder-2026');
const clubCurrent = canonicalRouteSummaryOf('clubsim-sms-pack-6hkd-2026');
const sosimCurrent = canonicalRouteSummaryOf('sosim-recharge-ladder-2026');

const guideRouteHref = (r: any) => routeDetailHref(r) || `${GUIDE_BASE}?route=${encodeURIComponent(r.id)}`;
const keepAliveHref = (r: any) => hasRouteDetail(r) ? `${GUIDE_BASE}keep-alive/${r.id}/` : `${GUIDE_BASE}keep-alive/#${r.id}`;
---
<GuideArticle slug="hong-kong-sim-retention-guide"
  h1="Hong Kong SIM retention guide"
  title="Hong Kong SIM retention: ClubSIM, SoSIM and eligibility (2026)"
  desc="Compare ClubSIM and SoSIM retention options, current pack eligibility, KYC and contradictory Telegram verification reports; no overseas OTP guarantee."
  lead="Hong Kong real-mobile SIMs can look inexpensive to keep, but acquiring one, passing real-name registration, preserving the line and receiving a named-app code abroad are different requirements. Check source-backed caveats before choosing a product.">

{club && <section class="gd-sec"><h2>ClubSIM — conditional HKD 6 retention research</h2>
<p>{club.acquisitionSummary || 'ClubSIM (HKT) prepaid with eSIM option.'}</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Keep-alive:</strong> {club.keep?.action || ''}</li>
<li><strong>Annual cost model:</strong> HKD {clubCurrent?.metrics?.keepYearCostOriginal} for the reported 365-day service-pack clock, when eligible. The current official web offer also advertises an HKD 6/30-day SMS pack; the historic yearly model is not a universal plan price or guaranteed checkout path.</li>
<li><strong>Window:</strong> {clubCurrent?.metrics?.keepIntervalDays} days for the documented service-pack purchase-clock interpretation; confirm exact account eligibility.</li>
</ul>
<p>Real-name KYC is required. Telegram registration reports are mixed across independent originals; neither generic incoming SMS nor one successful verification is a universal guarantee. This is a <strong>research-only</strong> route, not a mainland-first purchase recommendation. <a href={guideRouteHref(club)}>Inspect ClubSIM sources</a> and use the <a href={keepAliveHref(club)}>deadline calculator</a> only after checking your account’s real renewal method.</p></section>}

{sosim && <section class="gd-sec"><h2>SoSIM — the convenience-store alternative</h2>
<p>{sosim.acquisitionSummary || 'SoSIM (3HK) sold in ParknShop/Watsons.'}</p>
<p>The normalized record models {sosimCurrent?.metrics?.keepCurrency} {sosimCurrent?.metrics?.keepYearCostOriginal} per year under specific recharge assumptions. Verify real-name registration, which validity tier applies, first activation and overseas SMS reachability; do not infer app OTP compatibility from a store purchase.</p>
<p><a href={guideRouteHref(sosim)}>SoSIM route page</a></p></section>}

<section class="gd-sec"><h2>Which should you pick?</h2>
<p>Neither product is an automatic winner for someone who cannot complete the exact identity, purchase and first-activation requirements. ClubSIM may be cheaper to keep for eligible accounts, while SoSIM may be easier to find through retailers. Confirm the number type, eligibility, named-app SMS evidence and expiry/recovery conditions; then set your reminder for the <em>verified</em> active product.</p></section>
</GuideArticle>
